## Lessons from the 2026-08 burn (binding this burn)

See `docs/Proteus/paper_1_foundational/reference/burn_2026-08_swarm_retrospective.md`.

- **Every directive carries a kill criterion.** Each task in `SWARM_TASKS.json` names the
 observation that would falsify its premise. When it fires, the worker reports `BLOCKED`
 with the evidence and A1 abandons the family — no composition sweeps inside a dead one.
- **Refill by expected information, not by available parameter grids.** Decisive oracle
 / falsification experiments first; seed-fragile effect windows (works at seed 0, gone at
 1–2) are noise, not findings, and never justify a follow-up sweep.
- **Honest metric only:** sample-level background-aware ARI plus background recall and
 coverage on the shared normal-path sweep across seeds 0–4. Node-level component counts
 ("majors K=2") are not recovery.
- **Probes are disposable.** One-off diagnostic scripts stay under `/tmp` or are deleted
 before `DONE`; only reusable harnesses land in `tests/scenarios/`.
- **Acceptance-path constants** stay derived / calibrated by a declared protocol
 (SI S14.3); a worker may propose a constant only with its protocol and null envelope.

## Testing integrity

Never weaken tests to pass. Prefer flag-gated / proposed-path changes for acceptance-path
code. Run the relevant pytest subset before `DONE`.
